      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Sarangarh Secure</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Shipping a motorcycle from Sarangarh requires precise preparation to ensure a smooth, legally compliant, and secure transit. While Sarangarh is a smaller locale, the standards for commercial bike transportation remain rigorous. The foundation of any successful shipment lies in the proper documentation.</p>
<p>Without the correct paperwork, you risk delays, customs issues, or, worst-case, the seizure of your vehicle by authorities. Therefore, you must meticulously prepare and verify every document before handing over your bike to the logistics provider.</p>

<p>The most critical document is the <strong>self-attested photocopy of the Registered Certificate (RC)</strong>. This official document proves ownership and provides essential details about the vehicle, including its chassis number, engine number, and color. Ensure the copy is clear and legible.</p>
<p>Alongside the RC, you must provide a <strong>current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate</strong>. This certificate confirms that your bike meets the necessary environmental standards for emission, which is a mandatory requirement for road transport in India. An expired PUC can lead to immediate rejections at weighing bridges or police check posts.</p>

<p>Equally important is a <strong>valid insurance certificate</strong>. While your personal comprehensive insurance covers you during regular usage, it may not be sufficient for the specific risks involved in long-distance commercial freight. For this reason, you must also secure an <strong>IBA-approved Consignment Bilty</strong>.</p>
<p>This bilty acts as the official contract between you and the transporter, detailing the pickup and delivery points, the vehicle description, and the agreed-upon transit time. It serves as your proof of shipment and is essential for any claims.</p>

